{$mode delphi}{$H+}

{ GENERATED FILE — produced by tools/gen_fpc_mirror.py from
  tests/Integration/Kafka.IntegrationTests.pas (DUnitX). Do not edit by hand: edit the DUnitX
  master and run the script again. }

{ Integration tests against a real Apache Kafka 4.4.0 broker: the one-node
  KRaft broker of docker/docker-compose.yml (plaintext 9092, TLS 9093 with
  pascal-common-faa's test PKI).

  The K1 foundation's milestone (docs/design.md, section 7): connect,
  negotiate ApiVersions and read Metadata of a topic, in plaintext and over
  TLS with a private CA, on every TLS backend the platform has (SChannel and
  OpenSSL on Windows, OpenSSL elsewhere). Also: many requests in flight on one
  connection, a topic that doesn't exist, a CA that didn't sign the broker's
  certificate, a plaintext client on the TLS port (EKafkaProtocol at once,
  with a message that says the bytes look like TLS).

  Records: a batch written by this library (Kafka.Protocol.RecordBatch),
  produced to partition 0 and fetched back from the offset the broker gave
  it, in plaintext (uncompressed and snappy) and over TLS (gzip and lz4);
  the broker decompresses a batch to check it before it writes it, so a
  compressed batch it took is one Java's codecs read. ListOffsets sees the
  partition's end move. With acks=0 the broker sends no answer: the test
  asks for the partition's end first, then a Fetch from there with a
  MaxWaitMs, which the broker holds until the record arrives (no Sleep). Each
  record carries a marker of its own, so the tests don't depend on what
  earlier runs left in the topic.

  The cluster (Kafka.Cluster): a bootstrap past an address that isn't Kafka
  (the TLS port, in plaintext), the leaders of the topic's partitions on one
  connection per broker, the same over TLS, a topic auto-created on first
  use (a new name each run: the broker keeps them), and a keyed record sent
  to the partition murmur2 gives its key, through that partition's leader.

  The producer (Kafka.Producer): keyed records, gzip, acks=all, each in the
  partition murmur2 gives its key and fetched back from the offset its
  report gave; records without a key over TLS with acks=1, all on one
  sticky partition; and 20 000 records through Flush, every one delivered,
  in order within each partition.

  The consumer (Kafka.Consumer): every partition assigned and sought to
  its end, then records from the producer (keyed; gzip, snappy, and lz4
  over TLS; and uncompressed over TLS)
  polled back: each where the producer's report said, in order, with key,
  value and headers; a record produced from another thread while the
  consumer polls.

  The broker's address: KAFKA_TEST_HOST (default localhost), KAFKA_TEST_PORT
  (9092) and KAFKA_TEST_TLS_PORT (9093). The certificates: KafkaTestPkiDir.

  The topic (pascal-kafka-faa-it) is created by the broker on the first
  Metadata request that asks for it (auto-creation, on in the compose file);
  until its partitions have a leader the broker answers LEADER_NOT_AVAILABLE,
  so the first read retries for up to 30 s. That wait is on an external
  system, the one place these suites wait on time instead of an event.

  DUnitX master: the FPCUnit mirror in tests/Integration/fpc is generated by
  tools/gen_fpc_mirror.py. }

